      "content": "it was more than just kindness though. i could feel the ripple effect. when the atmosphere stabilized, the guy at the table next to me—who was already looking pretty agitated—actually relaxed and went back to his work. if that barista had snapped, that guy would've lost it too. it felt like one tiny lever moving a huge part of the whole street's momentum. do you see how those micro-shifts actually work? like how a single point of contact can prevent a much larger chain reaction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
